* which domain capabilities are exposed;
* tenant/workspace/project resolution;
* who may discover or invoke a capability;
* approval and confirmation for writes/destructive actions;
* idempotency keys and business-side deduplication;
* credential custody and deployment secret management;
* authorization-server policy and consent language;
* generic identity, login, signing-key, token-authority, and durable security-state policy;
* data retention for inspector traces;
* production smoke-test accounts and allowed side effects.

## Duplication inventory and consolidation rule

Current or likely overlap must be resolved deliberately:

| Area | Current overlap | Required outcome |
| -- | -- | -- |
| Production MCP client | LangFn implements its own official-SDK client, stdio/HTTP transports, pagination, result normalization, lifecycle, and error mapping | Move shared behavior into the McpFn production client; retain only temporary compatibility shims |
