::code-comment{title="[P1] Enforce provider authorization" body="The adapter calls authenticate but never invokes the AuthProvider resource-authorization contract. Existing deny policy is silently bypassed before trusted AuthInfo is constructed." file="/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/MCP-2/mcpfn/auth/src/provider-adapter.ts" start=43 end=50 priority=1}
::code-comment{title="[P1] Do not delegate the MCP token profile raw" body="Raw token and revoke callbacks leave grant parsing, token-auth negotiation, refresh/revocation behavior, and phase-specific error mapping in consumer code despite McpFn advertising those capabilities." file="/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/MCP-2/mcpfn/auth/src/hosted-authorization.ts" start=292 end=296 priority=1}
::code-comment{title="[P1] Revalidate metadata redirects and stream bodies" body="The allow policy covers only the initial URL; default redirects can cross that boundary, no timeout is applied, and the response is fully buffered before the byte cap is checked." file="/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/MCP-2/mcpfn/auth/src/hosted-authorization.ts" start=333 end=352 priority=1}
